  "thumbnailAlt": "Vendor Registration form beside a photo of a courier checking packages in a warehouse",
  "content": {
    "intro": "A vendor registration form is a form that collects a supplier's legal company details, tax ID, contacts, product categories and compliance documents so a procurement or accounts team can approve and set up the vendor. This template asks for documents like a W-9 and certificate of insurance up front, and it deliberately leaves out bank details so sensitive account numbers go through your finance system instead.",
    "audience": "Procurement teams, accounts payable, facilities managers, restaurants, construction firms, hospitals and event organizers onboarding suppliers and contractors.",
    "useCases": [
      "Adding a new raw-materials supplier to an approved vendor list",
      "Onboarding subcontractors who must show a certificate of insurance before site work",
      "Registering food, beverage or catering suppliers for a hotel group",
      "Collecting exhibitor and service vendor details for a trade show"
    ],
    "tips": [
      "Send each registration to Google Sheets or Microsoft Sheets so procurement and finance work from the same vendor list.",
      "Use conditional logic to ask for the W-9 only when the vendor says it is a US business.",
      "Allow edits with full edit history so you can see when a vendor updated their insurance certificate or address."
    ],
    "faq": [
      {
        "question": "What should a vendor registration form include?",
        "answer": "The vendor's legal name and trading name, business type, registration number and tax ID, address, primary and accounts contacts, products or services supplied, diversity or small-business status, and compliance documents such as a W-9 and certificate of insurance. This template covers each of these."
      },
      {
        "question": "Should I collect bank details in a vendor registration form?",
        "answer": "It is safer not to. Collect bank details through your accounting or AP system, or confirm them by phone with a known contact, because changed bank details in emails and forms are a common fraud route."
      },
      {
        "question": "What is a W-9 and do all vendors need one?",
        "answer": "A W-9 is the IRS form a US vendor uses to give you its taxpayer identification number. US businesses typically request it from US vendors they pay; foreign vendors usually provide a W-8 form instead. Check with your accountant for your situation."
      },
      {
        "question": "What is a certificate of insurance (COI)?",
        "answer": "A COI is a one-page summary from the vendor's insurer showing their coverage types, limits and policy dates. Many companies require one before a contractor works on site, and it should be renewed when the policy expires."
      }
    ]
  },
